</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>O what a peace it gives us</l><l>To see the sprinkled blood.</l><l>The blood of our peace offering</l><l>Has brought us peace with God.</l><l>With boldness we’re proclaiming—</l><l>Now hear this, enemy—</l><l>“Peace by the blood of Jesus!”</l><l>This is our victory.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Here God enjoys His portion—</l><l>’Tis inward, hidden, sweet—</l><l>And all the priestly family</l><l>May here the wave breast eat.</l><l>The offering priest—how precious—</l><l>May of the best partake:</l><l>He gets the right heave shoulder</l><l>And one unleavened cake.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>How sweet to eat the wave breast,</l><l>The all-embracing love</l><l>Of Christ in resurrection!</l><l>It sets us all above.</l><l>What strength to eat the shoulder</l><l>Of the ascended One</l><l>And with the cake be nourished</l><l>To walk as He has done.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>With all the cleansed ones feasting,</l><l>How rich the Christ we eat!</l><l>Oh, this is true communion,</l><l>The only way to meet.</l><l>We bring our full thanksgiving</l><l>And e’en would make a vow—</l><l>We’re for the Lord’s recovery</l><l>As He is for us now.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
